  "note": "Kannada composes from twenty upward. Formal orthography fuses the two words - twenty-one is written ಇಪ್ಪತ್ತೊಂದು, not ಇಪ್ಪತ್ತು ಒಂದು - and this file emits the spaced form deliberately: what the phonemiser receives is orthography, and a spaced pair pronounces as two clear words rather than as a fusion this file would have to spell correctly ninety times. Whether that costs intelligibility is a question for the listening panel, not for an engineer's judgement; task W7.11 answers it and clears this flag. There is no permissively licensed Kannada voice, so this pack recognises and displays but never speaks.",

